// radioButtons(attrs: List<Attr<M>>, children: List<Element<M>>) -> Element<M>: an element of
// the class RadioButtons. A group of radio buttons with one selection (WinUI's
// `RadioButtons`). The items are shown as [`RadioButton`]s: an item that is a radio button is
// its own container, and another item is the content of a radio button. The selection is the
// selection of the items control (`SelectedIndex`, `SelectedItem`, `SelectionChanged`), kept
// with the checked state of the containers. The arrow keys move the focus and the selection
// within the group without wrapping, Tab enters the group at the selected button, and Ctrl
// with an arrow key moves the focus only. The template is the control theme of the WinUI theme
// (`Controls/RadioButtons.xaml`, from WinUI's `RadioButtons.xaml`), with the parts
// `PART_HeaderPresenter` and `PART_ItemsPresenter` (WinUI's `HeaderContentPresenter` and the
// `ItemsRepeater` `InnerRepeater`); the theme sets the items panel, a
// [`RadioButtonsPanel`](crate::primitives::RadioButtonsPanel) with the spacing of the
// resources `RadioButtonsColumnSpacing` and `RadioButtonsRowSpacing`. The Fluent and Simple
// themes have no template for it (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). The exclusive
// check is the radio button group manager's: the containers are the logical children of the
// group and have no group name, so checking one unchecks the others. The group itself only
// checks the container of a new selection, and unchecks the container of the old one when no
// container is checked instead (a cleared selection, or one whose container is not realized),
// which the group manager never does (WinUI's `Select` writes both containers). Missing
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, Input): WinUI's element factories and
// `DataTemplateSelector` as `ItemTemplate`.
fn radioButtons(attrs, children) = Element { elementType: 317, elementAttrs: attrs, elementChildren: children }
// radioButtonsPanel(attrs: List<Attr<M>>, children: List<Element<M>>) -> Element<M>: an
// element of the class RadioButtonsPanel. Lays out the radio buttons of a [`RadioButtons`] in
// columns of equal cells as large as the largest one, filling each column from the top, with
// as many columns as the available width and the `MaxColumns` of the group allow (WinUI's
// `ColumnMajorUniformToLargestGridLayout`). Deviation (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, Input):
// WinUI lays the buttons out with a layout of an `ItemsRepeater`; FerroUI's `RadioButtons` is
// an items control, and this panel is its items panel, set by the control theme of the WinUI
