// in the foreground stack panel clipped to the value, from the glyphs of a
// [`RatingItemFontInfo`] (the stars E735 and E734 of the symbol font by default, in the font
// of the control) or the images of a [`RatingItemImageInfo`]. A click or a tap sets the rating
// under the pointer, and clears it when it is the rating (with `IsClearEnabled`); the arrow
// keys, Home and End change it. Only the changes of the user raise `ValueChanged`. The
// template is the control theme of the WinUI theme (`Controls/RatingControl.xaml`, from
// WinUI's `RatingControl.xaml`), with WinUI's parts `RatingBackgroundStackPanel` and
// `RatingForegroundStackPanel`; the items take their size from the `FontSize` of the stack
// panels (`RatingControlFontSizeForRendering`) and their brushes from the theme. The control
// sets WinUI's visual states (CommonStates) as the pseudo-classes `:placeholder`,
// `:pointeroverplaceholder`, `:pointeroverunselected`, `:set` and `:pointeroverset` (Disabled
// is `:disabled`). The Fluent and Simple themes have no template for it
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). Missing (docs/porting/winui-controls.md,
// Input): the composition animations of the scale of the items (the scale is set when the
// pointer moves), and the focus engagement of the gamepad (`IsFocusEngagementEnabled`,
// GamepadA and GamepadB).
